hadiths[164]{hadithnumber,text}:
"235","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), ""Which was the first mosque built on the earth?"" He (peace be upon him) replied, ""Al-Masjid al-Haram (i.e., the Ka'bah)."" I asked, ""Then which one?"" He (peace be upon him) replied, ""Al-Masjid al-Aqsa (i.e., Bayt al-Maqdis)."" I asked again, ""What was the time span between the two?"" He (peace be upon him) replied, ""Forty years."" And (he said), ""Wherever you may be when the time for prayer comes, perform the prayer there, for that is (also) a mosque."""
"236","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, arrived in Madinah and stayed in a high part of the city, in a neighborhood called the quarter of Banu Amr bin Awf. He stayed there for fourteen days. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, called the people of Banu Najjar, and they came with their swords hanging. Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: It is as if I am seeing the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, at that moment; he was on his she-camel and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, was behind him, and the people of Banu Najjar were around him, until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, dismounted in the courtyard of the house of Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him. The blessed habit of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was that wherever the time for prayer came, he would pray there, even in the place where goats were kept. (Because goats are poor and there is no fear that they would cause harm.) After that, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, ordered the building of a mosque and called the people of Banu Najjar. They came, and he said to them: Sell me your garden for a price. They said: By Allah, we will not take the price of this garden; we seek its reward only from Allah (meaning, we desire the reward of the Hereafter, we do not need money). Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I will tell you what was in that garden; there were date-palm trees, graves of polytheists, and ruins. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, ordered that the trees be cut down, the graves of the polytheists be dug up and removed, and the ruins be leveled. The wood of the trees was placed towards the qiblah, and stones were set on both sides of the door. When this work began, the Companions would recite rajaz (poetry), and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was with them. They would say: O Allah! The best and most excellent goodness is the goodness of the Hereafter, so help the Ansar and the Muhajirin."
"237","Abu Salamah bin Abdur Rahman says that Abdur Rahman bin Abi Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by, so I asked him, ""How did you hear your father narrate about which mosque it is that was founded on piety?"" He said that my father (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I was present in the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), in the house of one of his wives, and I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Which is the mosque that Allah, the Exalted, mentions as being founded on piety?"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took a handful of pebbles and struck them on the ground and said, ""It is this mosque of yours,"" meaning the mosque of Madinah. (Abu Salamah bin Abdur Rahman, the narrator of the hadith, says:) I said, ""I also bear witness that I too heard your father, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), mention this mosque in the same way."""
"238","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a woman became ill, so she said: ""If Allah grants me recovery, I will go to Bayt al-Maqdis and pray there."" Then she recovered, so she prepared to go and came to Umm al-Mu'mineen Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her), greeted her, and informed her of her intention. Maymunah said: ""Eat the provisions you have prepared and pray in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'One prayer performed in this mosque is better than a thousand prayers performed in other mosques, except for al-Masjid al-Haram.'"""
"239","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to go to the Mosque of Quba riding and walking, and he would offer two units of prayer there."
"240","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Mahmud bin Labid (may Allah be pleased with him) that when Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to build a mosque, the people disliked this and wanted to leave the mosque as it was (i.e., as it was during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him). So Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise like it."
"241","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved places to Allah among the cities are the mosques, and the most disliked places to Allah are the markets."
"242","Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) says that there was a man from among the Ansar whose house was farther from the mosque than any other house in Madinah, and none of his family ever missed (congregational prayer) with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) (i.e., he would reach for every prayer). I felt pity for him and said to him, ""I wish you would buy a donkey so that it would protect you from the heat and the insects on the road."" He replied, ""By Allah! I do not wish that my house should be adjacent to the house of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).” This statement of his was hard on me, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called him, and he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) the same as he had said to me, and added, ""I want the reward for my steps."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Indeed, you will have the reward for that which you hope for."""
"243","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution at his home, then goes to one of Allah’s houses to fulfill one of Allah’s obligatory acts, then each of his steps will cause one sin to fall away and the other step will raise him one degree."
"244","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were praying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when he heard the sound of people’s footsteps. He said (i.e., after the prayer), ""What is your condition?"" They said, ""We hurried for the prayer."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Do not do that. When you come for the prayer, come calmly. Then whatever you catch (with the Imam), pray it, and whatever you have missed, complete it."""
"245","Lady Zainab al-Thaqafiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If a woman wants to go to the mosque, she should not even touch perfume."
"246","´Sayyida ‘Amrah bint ‘Abd al-Rahman (may Allah be pleased with her) heard from Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: If the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had seen the women of this age who adorn themselves, he would have prevented them from coming to the mosque, just as the women of Bani Isra’il were prevented. (The narrator) Yahya ibn Sa‘id asked the narrator Sayyida ‘Amrah (may Allah be pleased with her): O ‘Amrah! Were the women of Bani Isra’il prevented from coming to the mosque? She said: Yes."
"247","Sayyiduna Abu Humayd (or Sayyiduna Abu Usayd) رضي الله عنه narrates that the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said: When anyone enters the mosque, he should say, ""O Allah, open the doors of Your mercy for me,"" and when he leaves, he should say, ""O Allah, I ask You for Your bounty, that is, sustenance and the blessings of this world."""
"248","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I went to the mosque and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting among the people, so I also sat down. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Who stopped you from praying two rak‘ahs before sitting down? I replied: O Messenger of Allah! I saw you and the people sitting, so I sat down (as well). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any of you enters the mosque, he should not sit until he has prayed two rak‘ahs."
"249","Abu Sha’tha’ says: We were sitting in the mosque with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) when the muezzin gave the call to prayer, and a man stood up from the mosque and began to leave. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) kept looking at him until he went out. Then Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: This person has disobeyed Abul Qasim (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"250","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is that (if one spits) he should bury it in the earth."
"251","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said during the battle of Khaybar: Whoever eats this plant, meaning the garlic plant, should not come to the mosque."
"252","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats onions or garlic should keep away from us, or he said: should keep away from our mosque and sit in his house. Once, a pot containing vegetables was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he found a bad smell in it, so he asked: What has been put in it? When it was made known to him, he said: Take it to such-and-such companion. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that he also disliked eating it (because the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not eat it), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You eat it, for I converse with one whom you do not converse with (i.e., the angels)."
"253","Ma’dan bin Abi Talhah narrates that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered a sermon on Friday and mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), and said: I saw in a dream that a rooster pecked me three times. I interpret this as meaning that my death is now near. Some people say to me that you should appoint your successor and caliph, and surely Allah Almighty will not ruin His religion, nor His caliphate, nor that which He sent the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with. If my death comes soon, then the caliphate will remain among those six people with whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was pleased until his death, through consultation. And I know that some people criticize those whom I myself struck with this hand of mine for the sake of Islam. Then if they do so (i.e., consider that criticism valid), they are enemies of Allah and disbelieving deviants. And after me, I do not leave anything as difficult as the matter of kalalah. I did not ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about anything as many times as I asked about kalalah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not show me such strictness in any matter as he did in this, until he poked me in the chest with his finger and said: O Umar! Is not that verse sufficient for you which was revealed in the summer at the end of Surah An-Nisa: “They ask you for a legal verdict. Say: Allah directs (thus) about al-Kalalah: If a man dies, leaving no child but (only) a sister, she shall have half of what he left...” (An-Nisa: 176). And if I remain alive, I will give such a verdict about kalalah that everyone will judge accordingly, whether he has read the Qur’an or not. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Allah! I make You a witness over those people to whom I have given the governance of lands (i.e., deputies, governors, and scholars). I have sent them only so that they may do justice, teach people the matters of religion, teach them the way of your Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), distribute the spoils of war among the people, and if they face any difficulty in any matter, they should ask me about it. Then, O people! I see that you eat two plants, and I dislike them—they are onions and garlic. And I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that when their smell came from any person, by the order of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he was taken out of the mosque towards Baqi’. Now, if anyone eats them, he should cook them well (so that their smell is eliminated)."
"254","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever hears someone calling out in the mosque about a lost item (that is, he raises his voice calling people for his lost thing), then he should say: May Allah not return your item to you. For indeed, mosques were not built for this purpose."
"255","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said that when the time of the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings be upon him) death approached, he began to cover his face with a striped cloak. When he would feel uneasy, he would remove the cloak from his face. In that state, he said: ""May Allah's curse be upon the Jews and Christians who took the graves of their prophets as places of worship."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) was warning that his own people should not do the same."
"256","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): Lady Umm Habiba and Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with them both) mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) a church which they had seen in Abyssinia, and in it were pictures. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: These people, when a righteous man among them died, they would build a mosque over his grave and make images in it. These are the worst of creatures in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection."
"257","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given superiority over the prophets in six matters: 1. I have been given words which are concise but have vast meanings (i.e., the Word of Allah or the words of the Messenger of Allah himself), 2. I have been helped by awe (cast into the hearts of my enemies), 3. The spoils of war have been made lawful for me, 4. The whole earth has been made a means of purification and a place of prayer (a mosque) for me, 5. I have been sent to all of creation (whether they are jinn, Arabs, or non-Arabs), 6. Prophethood has been sealed with me."
"258","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any one of you stands for prayer and there is an object in front of him equal to the back part of a saddle, then that is sufficient as a barrier for him. If there is not an object of that size (or higher) in front of him, and a donkey, a woman, or a black dog passes in front of him, then his prayer is invalidated. I said: O Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him)! What is special about a black dog, and not a red or yellow dog? He said: O my nephew! I also asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) just as you have asked me, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The black dog is a devil."
"259","Sahl bin Sa’d al-Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand for prayer at such a distance from the qiblah wall that there was enough space for a goat to pass through."
"260","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her)’ (when it was mentioned before her that the prayer is broken if a dog, donkey, or woman passes in front of the one praying) she said: You have made us equal to donkeys and dogs. By Allah, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying while I was lying on the bed in front of him, facing the qiblah. When I needed something, I disliked sitting up in front of him and causing him discomfort, so I would quietly slip away from the foot of the bed."
"261","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man entered the mosque and performed prayer while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was sitting in a corner of the mosque. Then, after narrating the entire hadith, he said at the end: When you stand for prayer, perform ablution properly, then stand facing the Qiblah, and then say the Takbir."
"262","´Sayyiduna Bara’ bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I offered prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) facing Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months, until this verse was revealed in Surah al-Baqarah: “Wherever you are, turn your faces towards the Ka‘bah” (al-Baqarah: 144). So this verse was revealed when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had already performed the prayer. One of his companions heard this and went out; on the way, he found some people from the Ansar (as usual) praying facing Bayt al-Maqdis, so he narrated this hadith to them (that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had been commanded to face the Ka‘bah). Upon hearing this, those people turned themselves towards the Ka‘bah during their prayer."
"263","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: When the takbir for the obligatory prayer is pronounced, then there is no (other) prayer except that obligatory prayer. Sayyiduna Bara’ bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I offered prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) facing Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months, until this verse was revealed in Surah al-Baqarah: “Wherever you are, turn your faces towards the Ka‘bah” (al-Baqarah: 144). So this verse was revealed after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had already performed the prayer. One of his companions, upon hearing this, went out and found some people from the Ansar (as usual) praying towards Bayt al-Maqdis. He narrated this hadith to them (that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had been commanded to face the Ka‘bah). Upon hearing this, they turned themselves towards the Ka‘bah while still in prayer."
"264","´Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When the call for prayer (iqamah) is made, do not stand up until you see me. (Do not stand before the imam arrives.) Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) facing Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months, until this verse was revealed in Surah al-Baqarah: ""Wherever you are, turn your face towards the Ka'bah"" (al-Baqarah: 144). So this verse was revealed after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had already performed the prayer. One of his companions, upon hearing this, went out and found some people from the Ansar (as usual) praying towards Bayt al-Maqdis. He narrated this hadith to them (that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had been commanded to face the Ka'bah). Upon hearing this, they turned themselves towards the Ka'bah while still in prayer."
"265","Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that when the time of decline (of the sun) would come, Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) would call the adhan but would not say the iqamah until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived and Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) saw him, then he would say the takbir (iqamah)."
"266","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Salamah bin Abdur Rahman bin Awf that he heard Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying that once the call for prayer (iqamah) was given and we straightened the rows before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out, and when he stood at his place and had not yet said the opening takbir, he remembered something and returned. He said to us, ""Remain standing in your places."" We all remained standing, waiting for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to return. He came after performing ghusl, and water was dripping from his blessed head (due to the ghusl). Then he said the takbir and led us in prayer."
"267","Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that for prayer, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would pass his hand over our shoulders and say: ""Stand straight and do not move forward or backward, otherwise discord will arise in your hearts. Also, let those who are very wise and intelligent stand closest to me, and then those who are next to them."" After this, Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Today, countless differences have arisen among you people."""
"268","Narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew the reward and merit of the call to prayer and standing in the first row, and there was no other way but to draw lots, then they would draw lots for it. And if people knew the virtue of offering prayer at its earliest time, they would compete with each other for it. And if they knew the excellence of 'Isha and Fajr prayers, they would come to them even if they had to crawl."
"269","`Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The best rows among men are the first rows and the worst are the last rows, and for women, the worst rows are the first rows (when the men's rows are close to them) and the best rows are the last rows (which are farther from the men)."
"270","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: If it were not difficult for the Muslims—and in Zuhair’s narration, it is stated: If it were not difficult for my Ummah—I would have commanded them to use the miswak at the time of every prayer."
"271","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came and joined the row for prayer while he was out of breath, so he said, ""All praise is for Allah, abundant praise, pure and blessed."" Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had finished the prayer, he said: Who among you said these words? So all the people remained silent. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) asked again: Who said these words? For he has not said anything bad. So that man said: I came and I was out of breath, so I said these words. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I saw twelve angels competing with each other as to which of them would take these words up (i.e., to Allah, the Exalted)."
"272","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for prayer, he would raise both his hands up to his shoulders, then say Allahu Akbar, and when he intended to bow (for ruku'), he would do the same, and when he raised his head from ruku', he would do the same, but when he raised his head from prostration (sajdah), he would not do so, meaning he would not raise both hands between the two prostrations."
"273","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would begin the prayer by saying Allahu Akbar and would start the recitation with “Alhamdulillahi Rabbil ‘Alamin” (meaning he would say Bismillahir Rahmanir Raheem quietly), and when he bowed (in ruku‘), he would neither raise nor lower his head but keep it level with his back, in between. And when he raised his head from ruku‘, he would not go into prostration (sajdah) until he stood up straight, and when he raised his head from prostration, he would not perform the second prostration until he sat up straight. After every two rak‘ahs, he would recite the Tashahhud (at-Tahiyyat) in the sitting position, spreading his left foot and keeping his right foot upright, and he forbade sitting like the devil and also forbade a person from spreading both hands on the ground like a wild beast, and he would end the prayer with salam."
"274","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand for prayer, he would say the takbeer, and then at the time of bowing (ruku‘) he would say the takbeer, and when raising his head from ruku‘ he would say: “Sami‘a Allahu liman hamidah,” and then while standing he would say: “Rabbana wa lakal-hamd,” and then when he would prostrate he would say the takbeer, and when raising his head from prostration he would also say the takbeer, and then until the end of the prayer, he would say the takbeer at every (sitting and rising). And after two rak‘ahs, when standing up, he would again say “Allahu Akbar.” After this, Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Among all of you, I perform the prayer most like the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"275","Sidna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, says that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, used to teach us and say: Do not do any action before the Imam; when he says the takbeer, then you say the takbeer; and when he says ""wa la ad-dallin,"" then you say ""Ameen"" after him; and when he bows (for ruku‘), then you bow after him; and when he says ""Sami‘ Allahu liman hamidah,"" then you say ""Rabbana lakal hamd"" after him."
"276","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` due to falling from a horse, the right side of the body of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was injured, so we went to visit him. Since it was time for prayer, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led the prayer while sitting, and we also prayed sitting behind him. When we all finished the prayer, he said: The Imam is appointed so that he may be followed; when he says the takbir, you also say the takbir, and when he goes into prostration, you also prostrate, and when he raises his head, you also raise your heads, and when he recites tasmi‘, you recite tahmid, and when he leads the prayer sitting, you also perform the prayer sitting. (This was the initial command; later, during the illness of death, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led the prayer sitting, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) prayed standing with him, and the companions prayed standing behind them.)"
"277","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Wa'il bin Hujr (may Allah be pleased with him) that he saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in such a way that when he started the prayer, he raised both his hands and said Allahu Akbar. (The narrator of this hadith, Hammam, states that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised both his hands up to his ears.) Then he put on his cloak, after which he placed his right hand over his left hand. Then, when he intended to bow (ruku‘), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took both his hands out from the cloak, raised them up to his ears, said the takbir, and went into ruku‘. And when, while standing, he said ""Sami‘ Allahu liman hamidah,"" he also performed the raising of the hands (raf‘ al-yadayn). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated between both his palms."
"278","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand in prayer, he would say: ""I have turned my face towards Him who created the heavens and the earth, being upright, and I am not of the polytheists. Surely, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living and my dying are for Allah, the Lord of all the worlds, who has no partner, and this I have been commanded, and I am of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the King, there is no deity except You, You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself and I confess my sins, so forgive all my sins, for none forgives sins except You. And teach me good habits, for none teaches them except You, and keep bad habits away from me, and none can keep them away except You. I am present for Your service and obedient to You, and all goodness is in Your hands, and nearness to You cannot be attained through evil (or evil alone is not attributed to You, for example, it is not said 'Creator of apes and swine' or 'Lord of evil', or evil does not ascend to You as the good word and righteous deed ascend to You, or no creature is evil for Your sake, even if it is evil for us because we are human, for You have created everything with wisdom). My success is from You and my supplication is to You. You are Most Blessed and Exalted. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance."" And when he would bow (in ruku‘), he would say: ""O Allah! I bow to You, I believe in You, and I submit to You. My hearing, my sight, my brain, my bones, and my sinews have all bowed to You."" And when he would raise his head from (ruku‘), he would say: ""O Allah! O our Lord! All praise is for You, filling the heavens, filling the earth, filling whatever is between them, and filling whatever else You will after that."" And when he would prostrate (in sujud), he would say: ""O Allah! I have prostrated for You alone, and I have believed in You, and I have submitted to You. My face has prostrated to the One who created it and fashioned it, and split its hearing and sight. Blessed is Allah, the Best of creators."" Then, at the end, between tashahhud and salam, he would say: ""O Allah! Forgive me for what I have sent forth and what I have left behind, what I have concealed and what I have made apparent, what I have transgressed, and what You know better than me. You are the First and the Last; there is no deity except You."" In another narration, it is mentioned that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would begin the prayer, he would say Allahu Akbar and then say: ""I have turned my face towards Him who..."" and recite until the end."
"279","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I have performed prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), Sayyiduna Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), Sayyiduna Umar al-Faruq (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), but I did not hear any one of them recite ""Bismillah ir-Rahman ir-Rahim"" aloud in the prayer."
"280","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that one day we were sitting in the gathering of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when a light drowsiness overtook him. Then, smiling, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his blessed head, upon which we asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What are you smiling at?"" He replied, ""Just now a surah of the Noble Qur'an has been revealed to me."" Then he recited ""In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful"" and recited the entire surah: '(O Noble Prophet [peace and blessings be upon him]!) Indeed, We have granted you Al-Kawthar...' and then said, ""Do you know what Al-Kawthar is?"" We said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He said, ""Al-Kawthar is a river which my Lord has promised me. It has many virtues, and on the Day of Resurrection, my followers will come to drink from this reservoir. There will be as many cups on this reservoir as there are stars in the sky. A person will be driven away from there, and I will say, 'O Allah! This person is from my followers.' Allah, the Exalted, will say, 'You do not know what new things (innovations) they introduced after you.'"""
"281","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: Whoever does not recite Surah Al-Fatihah in the prayer, his prayer is not complete, rather his prayer is deficient. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this sentence three times. The people asked, ""O Abu Hurairah, what should we do when we are behind the Imam?"" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: At that time, you should recite Surah Al-Fatihah quietly, because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say that Allah, the Exalted, has said: I have divided the prayer between Myself and My servant into two halves, and My servant shall have what he asks for. When the servant says, ""All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds,"" Allah, the Exalted, says: My servant has praised Me. And when (the worshipper) says, ""The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,"" Allah, the Exalted, says: My servant has extolled Me. And when (the worshipper) says, ""Master of the Day of Judgment,"" Allah, the Exalted, says: My servant has glorified Me, and He also says: My servant has entrusted all his affairs to Me. And when (the worshipper) says, ""You alone we worship and You alone we ask for help,"" Allah, the Exalted, says: This is between Me and My servant, and My servant shall have what he asks for. Then when (the worshipper) in his prayer recites, ""Guide us to the straight path, the path of those upon whom You have bestowed favor, not of those who have evoked [Your] anger or of those who are astray,"" Allah, the Exalted, responds: All this is for My servant, and whatever he asks for, it shall be given to him."
"282","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the mosque when a man arrived. After performing the prayer, he greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied to his greeting and said: ""Go and pray, for you have not prayed."" The man went back and prayed again as he had done before, then returned and greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""And peace be upon you,"" and said: ""Go and pray, for you have not prayed."" This happened three times. Then the man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""O Messenger of Allah! By Him Who has sent you with the truth, I do not know any better way than this, so please teach me."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you stand for prayer, first say Allahu Akbar, then recite whatever portion of the Qur'an is easy for you, then bow with calmness, then stand up straight with ease, then prostrate with tranquility, then sit with tranquility, and do this throughout your entire prayer."" (From this hadith, it is understood that maintaining calmness and composure in each posture of prayer is very important; without it, the prayer is not valid. According to the majority of scholars, maintaining calmness in each posture is obligatory.)"
"283","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the Zuhr or Asr prayer. Then he (peace be upon him) said: ""Who among you recited 'Subh-isma Rabbikal A'la' behind me?"" A man said: ""I recited this Surah and I intended good by reciting it."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""I know that some of you confuse me."" (Regarding this narration, Imam Nawawi (may Allah have mercy on him) has written that the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not prohibit recitation itself, but prohibited reciting aloud. And it is established in the hadith that the companion recited aloud, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: Who recited such-and-such Surah behind me?)"
"284","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Imam says Ameen, the followers should also say Ameen, and whoever's Ameen coincides with the Ameen of the angels, his past sins will be forgiven. Ibn Shihab (may Allah have mercy on him) stated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say Ameen after (the recitation of) ""wa la-d-dallin."""
"285","Simak bin Harb says: I asked Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) about the prayer of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform light prayers; he did not recite long surahs like those people, and in the Fajr prayer he would recite ""Qaf. By the Glorious Qur'an"" or surahs of similar length."
"286","`Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite Surah Al-Fatihah and another surah in the first two rak‘ahs of Zuhr and Asr, and sometimes he would let us hear a verse or so, and in the last two rak‘ahs he would recite only Surah Al-Fatihah."
"287","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, used to recite in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr, in each rak'ah, the equivalent of thirty verses, and in the last two rak'ahs, the equivalent of fifteen verses, or he said, half of that. And in the first two rak'ahs of 'Asr, in each rak'ah, the equivalent of fifteen verses, and in the last two rak'ahs, half of that (he used to recite)."
"288","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` (his mother) Umm Fadl heard him (Ibn Abbas) reciting Al-Mursalat 'Urfa, so she said, ""Son, by reciting this surah you reminded me that the last thing I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was this surah, as he recited it in the Maghrib prayer."""
"289","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) used to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then come to his own people and lead them in prayer. One night, after praying the 'Isha prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he came and led his people in prayer and started reciting Surah Al-Baqarah. A man turned away, said salam, prayed alone, and left. The people said, ""Have you become a hypocrite?"" He replied, ""By Allah, I am not a hypocrite. I will go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and tell him."" Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We are people with camels (we draw water from them all day), and Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) comes after praying 'Isha with you and starts reciting Surah Al-Baqarah."" Upon hearing this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, ""O Mu'adh! Are you a troublemaker? (Do you want to make people dislike the prayer and cause discord by reciting such long surahs?) Recite such-and-such surahs."" Sufyan said, ""I said to 'Amr that Abu Zubair narrated from Jabir that he said, 'Recite: Wash-shamsi wa duhaha, wad-duha, wal-layli idha yaghsha, sabbih isma rabbika al-a'la.'"" 'Amr said, ""Recite surahs like these."""
"290","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that one day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in prayer. When he finished the prayer, he turned towards us and said, ""O people! I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing, prostrating, standing, or in saying salam. I see you from in front and behind. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you were to see what I see, you would laugh little and weep much."" The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What have you seen?"" He replied, ""I have seen Paradise and Hell."""
"291","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever raises his head from prostration before the Imam should fear lest Allah transforms his face into that of a donkey."
"292","It is narrated from Aswad and Alqamah that we both came to Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them) at his house. He asked, ""Have those people (i.e., the nobles and leaders of that time) prayed behind you?"" We said, ""No."" He said, ""Get up and pray, because the time for prayer has come, and it is not necessary to delay your prayer while waiting for the nobles and leaders."" Then he did not order us to give the adhan nor the iqamah. When we began to stand behind him, he took our hands and placed one of us on his right side and the other on his left. When we bowed (in ruku'), we placed our hands on our knees. He struck our hands and joined our palms together, placing them between our thighs. When the prayer was finished, he said, ""Now your nobles and leaders will arise who will delay the prayer from its proper time and will constrict the prayer, until the sun is about to set (i.e., they will delay the Asr prayer so much)."" When you see them doing this, then pray your prayer at its proper time (i.e., at the best time), then pray again with them as a nafl (supererogatory) prayer. And when you are three people, all of you should pray together (i.e., stand in a row and the imam should be in the middle), and when there are more than three, one person should become the imam and stand in front, and when he bows (in ruku'), he should place his hands on his thighs and bend, and join both palms together and place them between his thighs, as if I am seeing at this moment the difference in the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"293","Mus'ab bin Sa'd narrates that I prayed next to my father and placed my hands between my knees, so my father said to me, ""Place both your palms on your knees."" Mus'ab said that then I did the same again, so he struck my hand and said, ""We have been forbidden from doing this and have been commanded to place both palms on the knees in (ruku')."""
"294","‘Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that’ the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his bowing and prostration, acting upon the Qur’an, would often recite this supplication: Subhanak Allahumma Rabbana wa bihamdika Allahumma ighfir li."
"295","´Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) lifted the curtain (during his illness before passing away) and the people were standing in rows behind Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O people! Now nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood (because prophethood has been concluded with me) except for righteous dreams which a Muslim sees or is shown. And know that I have been forbidden from reciting the Qur'an in bowing (ruku‘) and prostration (sujud); in ruku‘, glorify your Lord, and in sujud, strive in supplication, for it is more appropriate and likely that your supplication will be accepted."
"296","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would raise his head from bowing (ruku'), he would say: ""O our Lord, all praise is exclusively for You, as much as fills the heavens and fills the earth and fills whatever else You will after that (with praise). You are the Possessor of majesty and honor. The truest statement a servant has said—and all of us are Your servants—is: O our Allah! There is none who can withhold what You give, and none who can give what You withhold, and the effort of the earnest does not benefit them against You (rather, only what You will happens)."""
"297","Ma'dan bin Abi Talhah al-Ya'mari says: I met Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him), the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and I said to him, ""Tell me of an act by which Allah will admit me to Paradise,"" or he said, ""Tell me of the deed which is most beloved to Allah."" Upon hearing this, Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) remained silent. Then I asked him again, but he remained silent. When I asked him a third time, he said, ""I also asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) this question, and he said: 'Make frequent prostrations (sujood) to Allah, for you will not make a single prostration to Allah except that Allah will raise you one degree and remove from you one sin.'"" Ma'dan said: Then I met Abu al-Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked him the same question, and he gave the same answer as Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) had given."
"298","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant is closest to his Lord while in prostration, so make plenty of supplication in prostration."
"299","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones: on the forehead—and he (peace be upon him) pointed with his hand towards his nose—and on both hands, and on both knees, and on the toes of both feet, and I have been forbidden to gather up the clothes and hair."
"300","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Keep your limbs even in prostration, and none of you should spread his arms like a dog."
"301","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Malik bin Buhaina (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed prayer, he would separate his hands (from his sides) so much that I could see the whiteness of his armpits."
"302","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in prayer, he would place his left foot between his thigh and shin, and spread out his right foot, and place his left hand on his left knee, and his right hand on his right thigh, and would gesture with his finger."
"303","Tawoos says: We said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), ""What do you say about the sitting posture of Iq’aa?"" He said, ""It is Sunnah."" We said, ""We consider this sitting to be hard on a person (or on the feet)."" He said, ""(No), rather it is the Sunnah of your Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."" (Iq’aa is to sit with both feet upright and sitting on the heels.)"
"304","Hattan bin Abdullah al-Raqashi says that I was praying with Sayyiduna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him). When we were sitting in Tashahhud, someone from behind said that prayer has been made obligatory along with goodness and zakat. After the prayer, Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, ""Who among you said this?"" Everyone remained silent, so he (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""(You people are listening), tell me, who among you said this?"" When everyone remained quiet, he (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me, ""O Hattan! Perhaps you said these words?"" I said, ""No, I did not say them; I was afraid that you might get upset."" Then a person said, ""I said these words, and my intention was only goodness and virtue."" Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, ""You people do not know what you should recite in your prayer. Whereas the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has explained all matters to us during the sermon and taught us how to pray. That is, before you start the prayer, straighten the rows. Then one of you should become the imam, and when he says Allahu Akbar, you should also say it. And when he finishes 'wa la-d-dallin', you should say Ameen so that Allah is pleased with you. When the imam says the takbir and bows (ruku'), you should also say the takbir and bow, and after the imam's takbir and ruku', you should perform the takbir and ruku'. And do not perform the takbir and ruku' before the imam, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has said that your slight delay is counted as being equal to the imam's ruku' and takbirs. Then when the imam says 'Sami' Allahu liman hamidah', you should say 'Allahumma Rabbana wa laka al-hamd', and Allah hears your supplications, because Allah has said through His Messenger that whoever praises and glorifies Allah, Allah hears him. When the imam says the takbir and prostrates (sajdah), you should also say the takbir and prostrate, because the imam says the takbir and prostrates and rises a moment before you, and you perform these actions a moment after, so you will be with him. And when the imam sits in Tashahhud, each of you should recite this supplication: 'All verbal, physical, and financial acts of worship are for Allah alone. O Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is His servant and Messenger.'"""
"305","´Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the Tashahhud just as he used to teach us the Surahs of the Noble Qur'an, and he (peace be upon him) used to say: ""All verbal acts of worship that are blessed, and all physical acts of worship, and all financial acts of worship, all of them are for Allah. O Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon you), peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is His servant and His Messenger."" And in the narration of Ibn Rumh, it is mentioned that he (peace be upon him) used to teach (the Tashahhud) just as he used to teach the Qur'an."
"306","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate in prayer: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Dajjal, and I seek refuge in You from the trials of life and death, and I seek refuge in You from sin and debt.” A man asked, “O Messenger of Allah! Why do you so often seek refuge from debt?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “When a person is in debt, he tells lies and breaks promises.”"
"307","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah! Teach me a supplication which I may recite in my prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say, ""O Allah! I have greatly wronged myself, or committed much injustice against myself, and none forgives sins except You. So forgive me with forgiveness from Your presence, and have mercy on me. Surely, You are the Most Forgiving, Most Merciful."""
"308","Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up (for prayer), and we heard him saying, “I seek refuge with Allah from you.” Then he said, “I curse you as Allah has cursed you,” (he said this three times), and he extended his hand as if taking something. When he finished the prayer, we said, “O Messenger of Allah! Today in the prayer we heard you say things we had never heard before, and we also saw you extend your hand.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “The enemy of Allah, Iblis, came with a flame of fire to burn my face. I said three times, ‘I seek refuge with Allah from you.’ Then I said, ‘I curse you as Allah has cursed you, a complete curse.’ He did not retreat after the three times, so I wanted to seize him. By Allah, if it were not for the supplication of our brother Sulaiman (peace be upon him), he would have remained tied up till morning, and the children of Madinah would have played with him.”"
"309","Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were sitting with Sayyiduna Sa’d bin ‘Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) arrived. Sayyiduna Bashir bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, “O Messenger of Allah! Allah has commanded us to send blessings upon you, so tell us how we should send blessings upon you?” Upon hearing this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) remained completely silent, and we wished that he had not asked (Sayyiduna Bashir, may Allah be pleased with him). Then, after a short while, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Send blessings in this way: ‘O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and upon the family of Ibrahim, and send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and upon the family of Ibrahim in all the worlds. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.’ And the way of sending salam (peace) you already know.”"
"310","'Amir bin Sa'd narrates from his father, Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him), that I used to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) turning his face to the right and to the left while saying salam, to the extent that the whiteness of his cheek would become visible to me."
"311","'Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when we used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), at the end of the prayer we would say ""As-salamu Alaikum wa Rahmatullah"" to the right and to the left, while also gesturing with our hands. Upon seeing this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You gesture with your hands as if they are the tails of mischievous horses moving. It is sufficient for you to place your hands on your thighs in the sitting position and turn your face to the right and to the left, saying 'As-salamu Alaikum wa Rahmatullah.'"""
"312","Warrad, who was the freed slave of Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him), says that Sayyiduna Mughirah (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to Sayyiduna Mu’awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the prayer and said salam, he would say: “There is no true deity except Allah, He is alone and has no partner, sovereignty belongs to Him and all praise is for Him, and He is capable of everything. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the effort of the striver is of no benefit before You.”"
"313","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` we used to recognize the conclusion of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he would say Allahu Akbar."
"314","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: Whoever says (Subhan Allah) 33 times, (Alhamdulillah) 33 times, and (Allahu Akbar) 33 times after every prayer, these will be ninety-nine words, and completes one hundred by saying once (”La ilaha illallah wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul mulk wa lahul hamd wa huwa ‘ala kulli shay’in qadeer”), meaning “There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, He is alone, He has no partner, His is the dominion and for Him is all praise, and He is over all things competent,” then his sins will be forgiven even if they are as much as the foam of the sea (i.e., countless)."
"315","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` none of you should give a share to Satan from himself; do not think that it is obligatory upon me to turn only to the right after prayer. I have often seen that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would also turn to the left."
"316","'Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that' the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The one who knows the Qur'an most should lead the people in prayer. If they are equal in the Qur'an, then the one who knows the Sunnah most. If they are equal in the Sunnah, then the one who migrated earlier. If they are equal in migration, then the one who accepted Islam earlier. And do not lead in prayer in the place of authority of someone else (i.e., do not lead in the presence of the appointed Imam without his permission), nor sit on his seat in his house except with his permission."
"317","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he (peace be upon him) would go into bowing (ruku‘), the companions would also bow, and when he (peace be upon him) would raise his head from bowing, he would say: “Sami‘ Allahu liman hamidah,” and we would remain standing until we saw that he (peace be upon him) had placed his forehead on the ground; only then would we go into prostration (sajdah)."
"318","Sidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, says that a man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: ""I do not come to the morning congregation because so-and-so prolongs the recitation."" He said: ""I have never seen the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, so angry while giving advice as he was that day."" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""O people! Some of you make others dislike the religion. Whoever among you leads the people in prayer should keep it short, for behind him are the elderly, the weak, and those who have needs."""
"319","‘Ubaidullah bin Abdullah says: I went to Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) and requested, “Please tell me about the incidents during the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).” She said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fell ill, he asked, “Have the people performed the prayer?” We replied, “No, they are waiting for you.” He said, “Place water for me in a vessel.” We placed the water, and he performed ghusl (ritual bath). After that, he tried to walk but fainted. When he regained consciousness, he again asked, “Have the people performed the prayer?” We replied, “No, O Messenger of Allah! They are waiting for you.” He said, “Place water for me in a basin.” So we complied with his order, and he performed ghusl again. Then he prepared to walk, but again he fainted. When he regained consciousness, he asked again, “Have the people performed the prayer?” We replied, “No, O Messenger of Allah! They are all waiting for you.” Meanwhile, the people were all waiting in the mosque for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to come for the ‘Isha prayer. Finally, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent a message through a man to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) to lead the prayer. That man went to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, “The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has ordered you to lead the people in prayer.” Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) was very soft-hearted (he would start crying quickly), so he said to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), “O Umar! You lead the prayer.” Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, “No, you are more deserving of leading, and you have been ordered to do so.” Thus, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) led the prayer for several days. During this period, one day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) felt a little better, so he went to the mosque for the Zuhr prayer, supported by two men. One of these two men was Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who was his uncle. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) reached the mosque when Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) was leading the prayer as Imam. When he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he wanted to step back, but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gestured to him not to step back and said to those with him, “Seat me next to Abu Bakr.” So they seated him next to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) began to pray sitting, and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) continued to stand and follow the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), as if the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was the Imam and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) was the follower, and all the companions, as before, were following Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) in this obligatory Zuhr prayer. ‘Ubaidullah bin Abdullah narrates: I went to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and said, “I will narrate to you the hadith that Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated to me.” At his request, I narrated the entire hadith to him. After listening, he said, “This entire hadith is absolutely correct.” Then he asked, “Did Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) not mention the name of the other person who was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?” I replied, “No.” He said, “The other man was Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him).”"
"320","Narrated from Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) that I participated in the Battle of Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One morning, before the Fajr prayer, at the same place of Tabuk, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to relieve himself and I was with him carrying a water jug. After relieving himself, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, I poured water over his hands. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) first washed his hands three times, then washed his face. He tried to pull up the sleeves of his cloak to his arms, but the sleeves were tight, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his hands out from under the cloak and washed them up to the elbows, and then wiped over his leather socks. Then I set out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When we arrived there, we saw that Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) was leading the prayer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one rak’ah behind him. After Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) completed both rak’ahs and turned to say salam, he saw that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had stood up to complete his prayer with a second rak’ah. The Muslims became anxious upon seeing this and recited tasbih abundantly. Then, after finishing the prayer, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that you people did well. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expressed happiness that the people had performed the prayer on time."
"321","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a blind man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! I have no one to lead me to the mosque,"" and he sought permission from you (peace and blessings be upon him) to pray at home. So you (peace and blessings be upon him) granted him permission. Then, when he turned to leave, you (peace and blessings be upon him) called him back and asked, ""Do you hear the call to prayer?"" He replied, ""Yes."" So you (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then come to the mosque."""
"322","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer in congregation is twenty-five degrees superior to the prayer of a person alone."
"323","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that we used to think that (in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) only that hypocrite would stay behind from the congregational prayer whose hypocrisy was evident, or a sick person. And even a sick person, if he could, would come by placing his hands on the shoulders of two men and join the prayer. And he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) taught us matters of religion and guidance, and among those matters of guidance is to pray in a mosque where the call to prayer (adhan) is given."
"324","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Abi Amrah reports that Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the mosque after Maghrib and sat alone. I went and sat with him. He said, ""O my nephew! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Whoever offers the Isha prayer in congregation, it is as if he has spent half the night in prayer (i.e., he will receive such a reward), and whoever offers the Fajr prayer in congregation, it is as if he has spent the entire night in prayer."""
"325","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The ‘Isha and Fajr prayers are very heavy upon the hypocrites. If they knew the reward for them, they would come even if they had to crawl on their knees. And I had intended to order for the prayer to be established, then appoint someone to lead the people in prayer, and I would go with some men carrying bundles of wood to those who did not attend the prayer and burn their houses down. And in another narration, it is added: If a person were to find a meaty bone, he would surely come (i.e., to the prayer)."
"326","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I intend, regarding those people who do not attend the Friday (prayer), to order a man to lead the people in prayer, then I would go to the houses of those who did not come to Friday and burn them down."""
"327","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day after leading the prayer: ""O so-and-so! Why do you not perform your prayer properly? Does the one who prays not see how he is praying? Indeed, he prays for his own benefit. By Allah, I see those behind me just as I see those in front of me."""
"328","Sayyiduna Bara’ bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I observed the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and found that his standing, then bowing, then standing after bowing, then prostration, and the sitting between the two prostrations, then the second prostration, and the sitting between the prostration and the salutation—all of these were approximately equal."
"329","'Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that' Indeed, I do not fall short in praying with you in the manner that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray with us. (Thabit said) Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) used to do something which I do not see you doing: when he would raise his head from bowing (ruku‘), he would stand straight until someone would say that he has forgotten. And when he would raise his head from prostration (sajdah), he would remain so long that someone would say that he has forgotten. (That is, he would remain for a long time.)"
"330","`Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The best prayer among the prayers is the one in which standing is prolonged."
"331","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: ""I see you raising your hands as if they are the tails of unruly horses. Remain calm in prayer."" Then, on one occasion, he saw us sitting in circles and said: ""Why are you sitting separately?"" Then, on another occasion, he said: ""Why do you not form rows as the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?"" We asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! How do the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""They complete the first rows and stand close together in the row."""
"332","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me for some task. When I returned and reached him, he (peace be upon him) was riding (his mount). Qutaiba said that he (peace be upon him) was performing (nafl) prayer. I greeted him with salam, and he (peace be upon him) replied by gesture. When he finished the prayer, he called me and said, ""You just greeted me with salam, and I was performing prayer (so I could not reply verbally)."" Although his face was towards the east (and not towards the qiblah), (from this it is known that while performing nafl prayer on a mount, it is not necessary to face the qiblah)."
"333","Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Hakam Sulami (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I was praying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when one of us sneezed, so I said, ""May Allah have mercy on you."" The people started staring at me, so I said, ""May my mother weep over me (meaning, I wish I had died), why are you staring at me?"" Upon hearing this, the people began striking their hands on their thighs. When I saw that they wanted me to be silent, I became quiet. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, may my parents be sacrificed for him, I have never seen a better teacher before or after him than him. By Allah, he neither hit me nor insulted me, but rather said: ""Talking about worldly matters is not appropriate in prayer; it is only for glorification (tasbih), magnification (takbir), and recitation of the Qur'an,"" or as he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! My time of ignorance has just passed, and now Allah has granted me Islam. Some of us go to soothsayers (priests, astrologers)."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Do not go to them."" Then I said, ""Some of us take bad omens."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""That is something in their hearts, but it should not prevent them or you from doing anything."" Then I said, ""Some of us draw lines (i.e., on paper or the ground, as fortune-tellers do)."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""A prophet used to draw lines, so whoever draws lines like his, that is correct."" Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I had a slave girl who used to herd sheep towards Uhud and Jawaniyah (the name of a place). One day, when I went there, I saw that a wolf had taken away a sheep. After all, I am a man, and I get angry just as they do, so I slapped her. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) considered my action very serious. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Should I not free this slave girl?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Bring her to me."" I brought her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he asked her, ""Where is Allah?"" She said, ""In the sky."" Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""Who am I?"" She said, ""You are the Messenger of Allah (i.e., Allah has sent you)."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Free her, for she is a believer (i.e., she is faithful)."""
"334","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We used to talk during prayer; each person would talk to the one next to him while praying. Until this verse was revealed: ""Stand before Allah in silence (with obedience)."" From then on, we were commanded to remain silent and speaking was prohibited."
"335","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that men should say ""Subhan Allah"" and women should clap, and in one narration it is mentioned that (this should be done) in prayer."
"336","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Either the people must stop raising their gaze towards the sky while supplicating in prayer, or their eyesight will be taken away."
"337","It is narrated from Basar bin Saeed that Sayyiduna Zaid bin Khalid Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) sent him to Abu Juhaim (Abdullah bin Harith bin Simmah Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him) to ask what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had said about the person who passes in front of someone performing prayer. Sayyiduna Abu Juhaim (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If the one who passes in front of a person praying knew the burden (that falls upon him because of passing), he would consider it better to stand for forty than to pass in front of him. Abu Nasr said: I do not know whether (Abu Juhaim, may Allah be pleased with him) said forty days, or months, or forty years."
"338","Abu Salih al-Samman says: I was with Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him). He was performing prayer on Friday, separated from the people by a barrier. Meanwhile, a young man from the tribe of Abu Mu'ayt came and tried to pass in front of him. Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) struck him on the chest. The young man looked around and, finding no other way, again tried to pass in front of him. Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) struck him even harder. The young man stood upright and began to quarrel with Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him). Then people came and stopped him, after which he left and went to Marwan (who was the governor of Madinah) to complain. (The narrator says) Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) went to Marwan, and Marwan said, ""What did you do that your cousin is complaining about you?"" Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'When any of you prays behind a barrier and someone tries to pass in front of him, let him strike his chest; if he does not desist, then let him fight him, for he is a devil.'"""
"339","Sayyiduna Talha bin Ubaidullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We used to pray and animals would pass in front of us, so we mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace be upon him) said: If there is something in front of you equal to the back part of a saddle, then the passing of anything in front does not cause any harm."
"340","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would go out on the day of Eid, he would order a spear to be fixed in front of him. Then he would pray behind it, and the people would be behind him, and he used to do this while traveling as well. For this reason, the leaders have made it a practice (to keep a spear with them)."
"341","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would make his camel face the Qiblah and would pray towards it."
"342","‘It is narrated from ‘Awn bin Abi Juhayfah that his father, Sayyiduna Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him), saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a red leather tent. And I saw Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) bringing out the leftover water from the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and people began to rush to take it. Then whoever got the water rubbed it on his body, and whoever did not get it moistened his hand from his companion’s hand. Then I saw Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) bringing out a spear and fixing it in the ground, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), wearing a red garment and lifting it up to his shins, came out and stood facing the spear and led the people in two rak‘ahs of prayer. And I saw men and animals passing in front of the spear."
"343","`Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) forbade praying with one's hands placed on the waist."
"344","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saw spit in the mosque facing the qiblah, so he turned towards the people and said: ""What is the matter with you that one of you stands facing his Lord, then spits in front of himself? Does any one of you like that someone should face him and then spit in front of him? When any one of you feels the urge to spit, he should spit to his left under his foot, and if there is no place, then he should do like this (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, demonstrated this action)."" Qasim (who is the narrator of this hadith) stated that he spat in his garment and then rubbed that part of the garment together."
"345","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any one of you yawns during prayer, he should try to restrain it as much as possible. For indeed, the Shaytan enters (to cast doubts in the heart and make one forget the prayer). In another narration, it is mentioned: (When yawning) he should place his hand over his mouth. For indeed, the Shaytan (sometimes in the form of a fly or insect) enters (or in reality, the Shaytan enters, and this is correct)."
"346","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leading the people in prayer, and Umamah bint Abi Al-As (may Allah be pleased with her), his granddaughter, was on his shoulder (she was the daughter of his daughter Sayyidah Zainab, may Allah be pleased with her). When he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would bow in ruku', he would put her down, and when he stood up from prostration, he would lift her onto his shoulder again."
"347","Sayyiduna Mu’ayqib (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said regarding leveling the pebbles at the place of prostration, that if there is a need, one should do it only once."
"348","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Shikhkhir رضي الله عنه says that` I prayed with the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم, he spat, then rubbed it into the ground with his shoe."
"349","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he saw Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Harith praying with his hair tied in a knot, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) began to untie his knot. When he finished the prayer, he asked, ""Why did you touch my head?"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Whoever prays with his hair tied in a knot, it is as if he prays with his private parts uncovered."""
"350","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the time for prayer approaches and food is also served in front of you, then eat the food before the Maghrib prayer, and do not hasten towards the prayer leaving the food (because the heart will remain attached to the food, and there are other wisdoms as well)."
"351","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any one of you is uncertain in his prayer (about how many rak'ahs he has prayed) and does not know whether he has prayed three or four, then he should dispel the doubt and act upon what he is certain of. Then, before saying the salam, he should perform two prostrations. Now, if he has prayed five rak'ahs, these two prostrations will make it six rak'ahs, and if he has completed four, then by these two prostrations dust will be thrown in the face of Satan."
"352","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the Zuhr or Asr prayer, and after praying two rak‘ahs, he ended the prayer with salam. Then he came to a piece of wood that was fixed in the mosque towards the qiblah and stood by it, leaning against it in anger. At that time, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr as-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna ‘Umar al-Faruq (may Allah be pleased with him) were also present in the congregation. Both of them, out of fear, did not speak, and the hasty people left saying that the prayer had been shortened. Then a man, who was called Dhu’l-Yadayn (the one with two hands—although everyone has two hands, but his hands were long, so he was given this name), stood up and said, “O Messenger of Allah! Has the prayer been reduced or did you forget?” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), upon hearing this, looked to his right and left and said, “What does Dhu’l-Yadayn say?” The people said, “O Messenger of Allah, he is speaking the truth; you have only prayed two rak‘ahs.” Upon hearing this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed two more rak‘ahs and ended the prayer with salam. Then he said takbir and performed sajdah, then said takbir and raised his head, then said takbir and performed sajdah, then said takbir and raised his head. (Muhammad bin Sirin) said that ‘Imran bin Husayn narrated this to me and said that (at the end) he ended with salam."
"353","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would recite the Qur'an and come to a surah in which there was a verse of prostration, he would perform prostration, and those who were with him would also perform prostration, to the extent that some of us would not find a place to put our foreheads."
"354","Sayyiduna Abu Rafi’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I offered the ‘Isha prayer with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), and in it he recited “Idha as-samaa’un shaqqat” (the Surah), and performed a prostration in it. (After the prayer) I asked, “What kind of prostration did you perform?” He replied, “I performed this prostration behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and I will continue to do it until I meet him.” (Meaning, I will continue to do it for the rest of my life.)"
"355","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the recitation in the Fajr prayer, he would (in the second rak‘ah) raise his blessed head from bowing and say: “Sami‘ Allahu liman hamidah, O our Lord! All praise is for You alone.” Then, while still standing, he would say: “O Allah! Rescue Walid bin Walid, Salama bin Hisham, and ‘Ayyash bin Abi Rabi‘ah (all of whom were Muslims in the hands of the disbelievers), and the weak among the believers (i.e., those who were oppressed by the people of Makkah). O Allah, make Your grip severe upon (the tribe of) Mudar. And inflict upon them a famine like that in the time of Yusuf (peace be upon him) (as occurred in Egypt for seven years). O Allah, curse Lihyan, Ri‘l, Dhakwan, and ‘Usayyah (those who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger, peace and blessings be upon him).” Then news reached us that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) abandoned this supplication when the following verse was revealed: “O Prophet! You have no authority in this matter. Allah may accept their repentance or punish them, for they are wrongdoers.” __QUR_N__"
"356","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say, ""I will lead you in prayer as close as possible to the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" Then Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) would recite Qunoot in Zuhr, Isha, and Fajr, and he would supplicate for the believers and invoke curses upon the disbelievers.`"
"357","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Bara’ bin ‘Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite Qunoot in the Fajr and Maghrib prayers."
"358","Umm al-Mu’minin Hafsa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when dawn would break, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would not offer anything except two light rak‘ahs (i.e., the Sunnah of Fajr)."
"359","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The two rak'ahs of Fajr are better than the world and whatever is in it."
"360","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, recited ""Qul ya ayyuhal kafirun"" and ""Qul huwa Allahu ahad"" in the Sunnah prayers of Fajr."
"361","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) finished offering the Sunnah of Fajr, if I was awake, he would talk to me, otherwise he would lie down."
"362","Simak bin Harb says that I asked Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Did you used to sit with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" He said, ""Yes, very much."" Then he said that it was the blessed habit of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he would remain seated in his place of prayer after the morning prayer until the sun rose. Then, when the sun rose, he would stand up. And the people used to talk about the days of ignorance and laugh, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would smile."
"363","Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performing the Duha prayer. But I used to perform it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to like some actions but would not do them out of fear that if people started doing them, they might become obligatory."
"364","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: When a person enters the morning, a charity is due on every joint of his body. Then saying ""Subhan Allah"" once is charity, saying ""Alhamdulillah"" once is charity, reciting ""La ilaha illallah"" once is charity, and saying ""Allahu Akbar"" once is charity. Enjoining a good word is charity, forbidding an evil thing is charity, and performing two rak‘ahs of Duha prayer suffices for all these matters."
"365","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray four rak'ahs of the Duha prayer, and would add more as Allah willed."
"366","‘Abdullah bin Harith bin Nawfal says that I used to desire and inquire that someone would tell me whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the Duha (forenoon) prayer, but I did not find anyone who could narrate this to me except Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her). Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her), who is the daughter of Abu Talib, informed me that on the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came in the forenoon. A cloth curtain was put up for him, so he performed ghusl (ritual bath). Then he stood and performed eight rak‘ahs of prayer. I do not know whether his standing was long, or his bowing or prostration, (approximately) all were equal. And I did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performing the Duha prayer before or after this."
"367","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says that my friend (Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah! peace and blessings be upon him) advised me regarding three things: 1. Fasting three days every month. 2. Offering two rak'ahs of Duha (forenoon) prayer. 3. And performing Witr prayer before sleeping."
"368","It is narrated from Qasim Shaybani that Sayyiduna Zayd bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) saw some people performing prayer at the time of Duha, so he said: These people know well that prayer is more virtuous at a time other than this. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said that ""the prayer of the oft-returning (awabeen)"" is at the time when the feet of the young camels begin to burn (i.e., when the sun has risen high and the heat has intensified)."
"369","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When a person recites a verse of prostration and then performs prostration, Satan withdraws weeping to one side and says: Woe to him or to me! Man was commanded to prostrate and he prostrated, so Paradise is for him. And I was commanded to prostrate and I refused, so Hell is for me."
"370","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her) heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no Muslim servant who prays twelve rak‘ahs of Sunnah prayers for the sake of Allah every day, apart from the obligatory prayers, except that Allah builds a house for him in Paradise, or he said: a house is built for him in Paradise. Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Since that day, I have always performed them. And ‘Amr (meaning Ibn Aws) said: I have also always performed them since that day. And Nu‘man (meaning Ibn Salim) said the same. And in one narration it is: “Twelve rak‘ahs in one day and night.”"
"371","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughaffal al-Muzani (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There is prayer between every two calls to prayer (Adhan and Iqamah). He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this three times. The third time he said: Whoever wishes may offer it."
"372","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: I offered two rak‘ahs before Zuhr and two rak‘ahs after Zuhr (Sunnah) with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and two rak‘ahs after Maghrib, and two rak‘ahs after ‘Isha, and two rak‘ahs after Jumu‘ah. But the two rak‘ahs after Maghrib, ‘Isha, and Jumu‘ah, I offered with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at home."
"373","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Shafiq (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I asked Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) about the voluntary prayers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray four rak'ahs in my house before Zuhr, then he would go out and lead the people in the obligatory prayer, then come back home and pray two rak'ahs. He would pray Maghrib with the people, then come home and pray two rak'ahs. He would pray 'Isha with the people, then come home and pray two rak'ahs. And at night he would pray nine rak'ahs, in which was included the Witr. And he would stand and pray for a long part of the night, and sit for a long part of the night; when he recited while standing, he would also bow and prostrate standing, and when he recited while sitting, he would also bow and prostrate sitting. And when Fajr would come, he would pray two rak'ahs."
"374","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made a chamber out of palm leaves or a mat, and began to pray in it. Many companions came and started praying behind him. Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit says: Then one night, many companions came, but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) delayed and did not come out to them, and the people raised their voices towards him and threw pebbles at the door. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out to them angrily and said to them: If your condition had remained as it was, I feared that this prayer would also become obligatory upon you. Pray in your homes, for except for the obligatory prayer, a person's best prayer is that which he performs in his house (because it is free from showing off). In another narration, it is mentioned that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) made a chamber in the mosque with a mat."
"375","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When a person offers prayer in his mosque, he should save a portion to pray at home (i.e., Sunnah and Nafl prayers), because Allah will bring goodness to his house through his prayer."
"376","Narrated Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and saw a rope hanging between two pillars. He said, ""What is this?"" The people said, ""This is the rope of Umm al-Mu'mineen Zaynab (may Allah be pleased with her); she prays, and when she becomes sluggish or tired, she holds onto it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Untie it. Each of you should pray as long as he is energetic. When he becomes sluggish or tired, he should sit down."""
"377","Alqamah says: I asked Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), ""What was the state of the worship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? Did he specify any particular day for worship?"" She said, ""No, rather his worship was constant. And who among you can do the worship that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) could do?"""
"378","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that when Hawla bint Tuwait passed by in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""This is Hawla bint Tuwait, and people say that she does not sleep at night (engaged in worship)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do deeds according to your capacity. By Allah, Allah does not tire (of giving reward), but you will tire."""
"379","´Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` one night I stayed with my maternal aunt, Umm al-Mu’minin Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) (so that I could observe the Tahajjud prayer of the Prophet ﷺ). The Prophet ﷺ got up at night and went to relieve himself, then washed his hands and face and then lay down again. Then he got up, came to the water-skin and untied its string, then performed an ablution between two extremes (i.e., neither very thorough nor very light), and did not waste much water, and completed the ablution. Then he stood up and began to pray. I also got up and stretched myself so that the Prophet ﷺ would not think that I was alert just to observe his state (from this it is known that the Companions did not hold the belief of knowledge of the unseen for the Prophet ﷺ as the ignorant now do for the Prophets and saints). I performed ablution and stood on his left side. The Prophet ﷺ took my hand and turned me to stand on his right side. (From this it is known that if there is one follower, he should stand on the right side of the Imam.) In short, the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at night was completed in thirteen rak‘ahs, then he lay down and slept until he began to snore. And it was the blessed habit of the Prophet ﷺ that when he slept, he would snore. Then Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) came and informed the Prophet ﷺ about the morning prayer, so he got up and performed the (Sunnah of Fajr) prayer and did not perform ablution again, and supplicated with these words: “O Allah, place light in my heart, and light in my eyes, and light in my ears, and light on my right, and light on my left, and light above me, and light beneath me, and light in front of me, and light behind me, and increase light for me.” Kurayb (the narrator of the hadith) said that there were seven more words which are in my heart (i.e., they do not come to my tongue because I have forgotten them). Then I met some of the children of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), and they informed me that those words were: “my sinew, my flesh, my blood, my hair, my skin, and two other things” (i.e., in all these the Prophet ﷺ asked for light)."
"380","Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would begin the night prayer, he would first perform two light rak'ahs."
"381","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would stand for prayer at night, he would say: ""O Allah, all praise is for You alone. You are the Light of the heavens and the earth, and all praise is for You. You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth, and all praise is for You. You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and all that is in them. You are True, Your promise is true, Your word is true, meeting You is true, Paradise is true, Hell is true, the Hour is true. O Allah, I submit to You, I believe in You, I rely upon You, I turn to You, I argue with others for Your sake, and I seek judgment from You. So forgive my past and future sins, those I have done in secret and in open. O Allah, You are my God, there is no god but You."""
"382","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray thirteen rak'ahs at night. Among them were five witr, and he would sit only at the end (that is, he would pray five rak'ahs of witr with only one tashahhud)."
"383","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about the night prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The night prayer is (offered) two by two rak‘ahs. Then when you fear that dawn is approaching, pray one rak‘ah, for it will make what you have prayed an odd number."
"384","Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting (Qur'an) while sitting during the night prayer. But when he became old, he would recite while sitting, and when about thirty or forty verses of the surah remained, he would stand up and recite, then bow (ruku)."
"385","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` a man was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) who sleeps until morning (i.e., does not get up for Tahajjud), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said that Satan urinates in his ear or both his ears."
"386","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any one of you becomes drowsy during prayer, he should sleep until his sleep goes away. For when any one of you becomes drowsy, it is possible that he intends to seek forgiveness but starts cursing himself instead."
"387","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that: When one of you sleeps, Satan ties three knots at the back of his neck. On each knot he blows and says: ""The night is long, so sleep."" When he wakes up and remembers Allah, one knot is undone. When he performs ablution, two knots are undone. And when he prays, all the knots are undone. Then he rises in the morning energetic and in a good mood; otherwise, he gets up with a bad heart and lazy."
"388","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There is a moment during the night in which, if any Muslim asks Allah for goodness of this world and the Hereafter, Allah grants it to him, and this (moment) occurs every night."""
"389","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: When the first third of the night passes, Allah Almighty descends every night to the sky of the world and says: ""I am the King, I am the King. Who is there who supplicates to Me so that I may accept it? Who is there who asks of Me so that I may give to him? Who is there who seeks forgiveness from Me so that I may forgive him?"" Thus He continues saying this until the brightness of dawn appears."
"390","It is narrated from Zurara that Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Hisham bin ‘Amir intended to strive in the way of Allah, came to Madinah, and wanted to sell his land and gardens in Madinah so that he could buy weapons and horses with that money and fight the Christians until death. When he came to Madinah and met the people of Madinah, they forbade him (i.e., they told him that he should not completely abandon worldly affairs and human necessities), and informed him that during the lifetime of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), six men had intended to do this, but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade them and said, “Is my way not better for you?” When the people said this to him, he took back his wife, whom he had divorced, in the presence of witnesses. Then he went to Sayyiduna Ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and asked him about the Witr prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He said, “Shall I not tell you of a person who knows better than all the people of the earth about the Witr prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?” He asked, “Who is that?” Sayyiduna Ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, “It is Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her), so go to her, ask her, and then come and inform me of her answer.” Then I (Sa’d bin Hisham) left him and went to Hakim bin Aflah and asked him to take me to Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her). He said, “I do not go to her because I forbade her from speaking about those two groups (i.e., the internal conflicts among the Companions), but she did not listen and went ahead.” (Sa’d bin Hisham) said, “I made Hakim swear an oath, so he agreed, and we both went to Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) and informed her, so she gave us permission, and we presented ourselves before her.” Then she said, “Is this Hakim?” He said, “Yes.” Thus, Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) recognized him (i.e., by his voice, etc., from behind the veil). Then she asked, “Who is with you?” Sayyiduna Hakim said, “Sa’d bin Hisham is with me.” She asked, “Which Hisham?” Hakim said, “The son of ‘Amir.” Then she prayed for mercy upon him, and Qatadah said that he was martyred in the Battle of Uhud. Then I said, “O Umm al-Mu’minin! Tell me about the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).” She said, “Have you not read the Qur’an?” I (Sa’d) said, “Why not?” She said, “The character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was the Qur’an.” She said, “Then I intended to leave and decided not to ask about anything else until death. Then I thought and said, ‘Tell me about the night rising (and prayer) of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).’” Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said, “Have you not read ‘O you who wraps himself [in a garment]’ (Surah al-Muzzammil)?” I said, “Why not?” She said, “At the beginning of this Surah, Allah made standing in prayer at night obligatory. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and his Companions continued to pray at night, and Allah withheld the conclusion (last verses) of this Surah in the heavens for twelve months, until Allah revealed the end of this Surah and granted ease (i.e., the obligation of Tahajjud was lifted and it remained Sunnah). Then after the obligation of night prayer (Tahajjud), it became a matter of happiness (i.e., it became voluntary).” Then I said, “O Umm al-Mu’minin! Tell me about the Witr prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) as well.” She said, “We used to prepare the miswak and water for ablution for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and Allah would awaken him at night whenever He wished. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would use the miswak and perform ablution, then pray nine rak‘ahs. He would not sit except after the eighth rak‘ah, and he would remember Allah, praise Him, and supplicate (i.e., recite the tashahhud), then he would not say salam but stand up and pray the ninth rak‘ah, then sit, remember Allah, praise Him, and supplicate, and then say salam in such a way that we could hear it (so that those sleeping would wake up). Then after salam, he would pray two rak‘ahs while sitting; thus, these were eleven rak‘ahs. O my son! Then when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) grew older and his body became heavier, he started praying seven rak‘ahs of Witr, and he would pray the rak‘ahs as he did before. Thus, these were nine rak‘ahs. O my son (i.e., seven Witr and Tahajjud and two rak‘ahs after Witr). And it was the habit of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that whenever he prayed any prayer, he would be consistent in it, and when sleep or pain overcame him so that he could not get up at night, he would pray twelve rak‘ahs during the day (i.e., he would not pray Witr; from this it is proven that there is no qada for Witr). And I do not know that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ever recited the entire Qur’an in one night (from this, completing the Qur’an in one night is proven to be an innovation), nor do I know that he ever prayed the whole night until morning (i.e., without sleeping or resting at all), nor that he fasted an entire month except Ramadan.” Then I went to Sayyiduna Ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and narrated this entire hadith to him, so he said, “Indeed, Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) has spoken the truth.” And he said, “If I had been with her or had gone to her, I would have heard this hadith directly.” Sa’d said, “If I had known that you do not go to her, I would never have told you her words.”"
"391","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Witr in the early part of the night, in the middle, and in the last part of the night, up until the time of Fajr."
"392","Sayyiduna Anas bin Sirin (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) to tell me about the two rak‘ahs before the Fajr prayer—should I recite long (Qira’at) in them? Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray two rak‘ahs at night and would pray one rak‘ah as Witr. (Ibn Sirin) says: I said, “That is not what I am asking.” Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “You are a heavy man (meaning, of heavy intellect, as you interrupted in the middle of the narration). Will you not give me the chance to narrate the whole hadith?” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to pray two rak‘ahs at night, and one as Witr, and he would pray two rak‘ahs before the obligatory Fajr prayer at such a time that the takbir would be in his ear (i.e., he would pray them at the time of the takbir, and obviously, the prayer at that time would be very light)."
"393","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever fears that he may not be able to get up at the end of the night should perform Witr in the early part of the night (after ‘Isha). And whoever hopes to get up at the end of the night should perform Witr at the end of the night, because the prayer at night is such that angels are present in it, and it is superior."
"394","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform Witr before dawn."
"395","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Does any one of you like that when he returns to his house, he finds three large pregnant she-camels in it?"" We said, ""Yes."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""For any one of you, reciting three verses in prayer is better than three large, swift, pregnant she-camels."""
"396","‘Sayyiduna Abu Wa’il (may Allah be pleased with him) says: One day, after offering the Fajr prayer, we went early in the morning to the house of Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them). We stood at the door and greeted with salam, and we were granted permission. Abu Wa’il says: We stood at the door for a little while, then a girl came out and said, “Why do you not enter inside?” So we entered and saw that Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them) was sitting and reciting tasbih. He said, “When you were given permission, what prevented you from entering?” We said, “Nothing, we just thought that perhaps some of your family members might be asleep.” Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them) said, “Did you think the family of Ibn Umm ‘Abd to be heedless?” Then he became engaged in tasbih again until he thought that the sun had risen. He said to the girl, “Look, has the sun risen?” Abu Wa’il says: She looked and said, “No, the sun has not yet risen.” He again became engaged in tasbih until he thought that the sun had risen. He again said to the girl, “Look, has the sun risen?” She looked and said, “Yes, the sun has risen.” He said, “All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds, who has forgiven us in this day of ours.” Mahdi says: I think Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them) said, “And did not destroy us because of our sins.” Then a man from among the people said, “I have recited all the Mufassal surahs this night.” Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them) said, “You recited like poetry is recited.” We have indeed heard the pairs, and I remember those pairs which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite. They are eighteen surahs from the Mufassal and two surahs from Al-Ha-Meem. (By pairs, it is meant those surahs which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite two at a time in one rak’ah.)"
"397","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out (approximately) at midnight and prayed in the mosque, and a few people prayed with him. Then in the morning, people began to talk about it, and the next day more people gathered. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also came out, then people prayed with him, and in the morning people began to talk about it. Then on the third night, more people gathered in the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, and people prayed with him. Then when the fourth night came and so many people gathered that the mosque became crowded, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not come out, people began to call out, “Prayer, prayer,” but he did not come out until he came for the morning prayer. Then when he had finished the prayer, he turned to the people, recited the two testimonies, and after praise and blessings, said: “Know that your condition tonight was not hidden from me, but I feared that the night prayer (Tarawih) might be made obligatory upon you and you would be unable to perform it.” And in one narration, it is mentioned that this incident took place in Ramadan."
"398","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to encourage the offering of Tarawih prayers in Ramadan, but did not make it obligatory. He said: Whoever prays during Ramadan with faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and the matter remained as it was. The same practice continued during the caliphate of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). And in the early period of the caliphate of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), the same method remained (i.e., whoever wished would pray at night)."
